1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:04,305
Your engine can set off six thousand explosions… every minute.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,365
So how does a car actually move?

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,175
Let's look inside the engine.

4
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:12,405
Every cylinder runs four steps.

5
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:15,370
Suck. The piston drops, pulling in air and fuel.

6
00:00:16,625 --> 00:00:20,190
Squeeze. It rises, crushing the mix about ten times smaller.

7
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,095
Bang! A spark of up to forty thousand volts ignites it.

8
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:27,790
Blow. The piston pushes the burnt gas out the exhaust.

9
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:30,575
Suck. Squeeze. Bang! Blow.

10
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:31,935
Thousands of times a minute.

11
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:35,835
Four cylinders take turns firing, spinning the crankshaft.

12
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,435
Rev it to three thousand RPM.

13
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,295
That's a hundred explosions a second.

14
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:44,355
Gears trade force for speed: low to launch, high to cruise.

15
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:48,405
Turning? Outer wheels go farther, so the differential lets them spin faster.

16
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:49,705
How much fuel moves you?

17
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:50,925
About twenty percent.

18
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,345
The rest? Mostly heat.

19
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:55,155
Fuel. Bang! Spin. Gears. Wheels.

20
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:56,445
Every time you hit the gas.

21
00:00:56,850 --> 00:00:58,695
Follow for more amazing facts.
